Subject: [PATCH] sftp: free the INIT message sftp_server_init() reads

sftp_server_init() reads the client's SSH_FXP_INIT with
sftp_get_client_message() and never frees it, on success or on either
error path: the message and its two buffers, about 190 bytes, for every
SFTP session a server accepts. Found by LeakSanitizer in BeerSSH's
SFTP-only server, which answers INIT this way because the callback
server's handlers are the unconfined defaults it exists not to use.

Free it once sftp_reply_version() has used it, and before returning on
a packet of the wrong type.

--- a/src/sftp.c
+++ b/src/sftp.c
@@ -289,12 +289,14 @@
                       SSH_FATAL,
                       "Packet read of type %d instead of SSH_FXP_INIT",
                       msg->type);
+        sftp_client_message_free(msg);
         return -1;
     }
 
     SSH_LOG(SSH_LOG_PACKET, "Received SSH_FXP_INIT");
 
     rc = sftp_reply_version(msg);
+    sftp_client_message_free(msg);
     if (rc != SSH_OK) {
         ssh_set_error(session,
                       SSH_FATAL,
